invariant: INV-38
file: handshake.c
catches: test/handshake_sequence_shards.sh ./bin/handshake_sequence_test
builds: bin/handshake_sequence_test
reason: the blocking client sends its record_size_limit in the ClientHello
  but leaves ch_tls.limit_sent clear, so a server record over that limit
  gets internal_error, not the record_overflow RFC 8449 §4 requires. The
  sequence test's MUT_REC_OVER case reads the alert on the wire.

--- old
    t->limit_sent = 1;
    t->peer_limit = CH_TX_PT;
--- new
    t->peer_limit = CH_TX_PT;
